      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 1460,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Smoke tests, demos and Q&A (40)\n\nTest fixtures and worked examples. Most were last changed on 14 or 15 October. They are fine to leave, and are the first place to look if something old breaks.\n\n- Class Smoke Test (yours graphs/class-smoketest)\n- Navigation today (yours graphs/navigation-today)\n- Page looks (yours graphs/page-looks)\n- Interaction Arbiter Smoke Test (yours graphs/interaction-arbiter-smoke)\n- Semantic Zoom Fallback Smoke Test (yours graphs/semantic-zoom-fallback-smoke)\n- New graph (yours graphs/fixture-b)\n- New graph (yours graphs/fixture-a)\n- Cross-Graph Interaction and Data Handoff (yours graphs/inter-graph-data-handoff-plan)\n- Example Note Smoke Test (yours graphs/example-note-smoke)\n- Exposed Port Navigation Plan (yours graphs/exposed-port-navigation-plan)\n- Graph Lab (yours graphs/root)\n- How Will Graph-Based Interfaces Change the Web? (yours qa/how-will-graph-based-interfaces-change-the-web)\n- Multiple Installed Workboards Smoke Test (yours graphs/template-installation-multiple-workboards)\n- Script Capability Placement Smoke (yours graphs/script-capability-smoke)\n- Template Installation Smoke Test (yours graphs/template-installation-smoke)\n- Twilite (demo) (yours graphs/twilite-demo)\n- Twilite Is the Matrix (yours graphs/twilite-matrix-browser)\n- Twilite Workspace Persistence (yours qa/workspace-persistence)\n- View Model Simplification Plan (yours graphs/view-model-simplification-plan)\n- What Is Twilite? (yours qa/what-is-twilite)\n- Who Is Twilite For? (yours qa/who-is-twilite-for)\n- Canvas Smoke Test (yours graphs/canvas-smoke-test)\n- Composition Smoke Node (yours graphs/interface-frame-smoke)\n- Declaration Primary View Toolbar Smoke (yours graphs/declaration-primary-view-toolbar-smoke)\n- Edge and Label Navigation Smoke Test (yours graphs/edge-label-navigation-smoke)\n- Episode Structure Map (yours graphs/candace-owens-episode-Ep360)\n- Folder Contents (yours graphs/folder-contents)\n- How Should Focus Work in Twilite? (yours qa/focus-model-spec)\n- Indiana Jones (yours graphs/indiana-jones)\n- Plate Tectonics (yours graphs/plate-tectonics)\n- Primitive Port Layouts (yours qa/primitive-port-layouts)\n- Primitive Port Layouts — Smoke Test (yours qa/primitive-port-layouts-smoke)\n- Q&A Collection (yours qa/root)\n- The Boulevard (demo) (yours graphs/boulevard-demo)\n- The Commons (demo) (yours graphs/commons-demo)\n- The Water Cycle (yours graphs/watercycle)\n- The water cycle (scene demo) (yours graphs/water-cycle-demo)\n- Twilite Front Door Smoke (yours graphs/twilite-front-door-smoke)\n- Twilite: A Graph-Native World (yours graphs/twilite-overview)\n- Wheel and Zoom Test Bench (yours qa/wheel-test-bench)"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-map",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "What this session touched",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8100
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 380,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# What the recent work touches\n\nThe work of the last few days, and the older graphs it probably belongs to. This is my reading, not something the graphs say, so check each pairing before closing anything.\n\n- **Handles** (drawn on workspace tiles, dragging, the plain 8-ball, art on the border, hover-only signs) → `tasks/ports-and-handles-interface` (yours, in progress) and the canon smoke suite `tasks/graph-defined-handle-smoke-suite`. The first has 5 done, 2 in progress and 1 to do, and has not been updated since. Its tasks may be done now.\n- **Primitive pages, posters, small-tile scaling** → `tasks/canon-templates-in-order` (5 done, 7 to do) and `tasks/canon-view-shape-consistency` (1 blocked), plus the new `tasks/primitives-self-documenting`. Canon's own `tasks/primitive-library` is done.\n- **Authoring switches and the Properties panel** → canon `tasks/authoring-contract-hardening` (open, 4 to do, 2 open questions) is the nearest older plan, and `tasks/property-node-inline-editor` (yours, 6 in progress) is the nearest old work on the editing surface. The new `tasks/properties-and-authoring-contract` is the one to keep; those two may fold into it or close.\n- **Workspace** (tile handles, scope, drag) → `tasks/workspace-graph-space-unification` (3 in progress), `tasks/workspace-save-connection-validation` (2 in progress), and canon `tasks/workspace-graph-node-projection` and `tasks/workspace-bridge-apertures`."
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "where-i-am-triage",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "A way to sort it",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8520
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 470,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# A way to sort it\n\nA proposal, to edit. Nothing here has been done.\n\n1. **Archive what is finished** (15 task graphs). It costs nothing and takes the list from 76 to 61.\n2. **Close or fold in what the recent work overtook.** Start with the three pairings above: handles, the Properties panel, and canon's `authoring-contract-hardening`.\n3. **Decide the 15 October burst as a set**, not one at a time. It is one program (Methods, events, Bridges, the workspace), 29 task graphs started and 26 not. Either it is a stream you still intend to pick up, in which case it needs a single front-door task graph, or it is background and can be parked.\n4. **Keep three streams open at once, no more.** At the moment these are: *primitives and templates* (canon-templates-in-order, primitives-self-documenting), *the Properties panel and the contract* (the new task graph), and *the workspace* (unification and save validation). Everything else waits.\n5. **Leave the ideas alone.** They cost nothing while they sit.\n\nThe question that decides step 3 is yours: is the Methods, events and Bridges program still the next big thing after the templates, or has the work of the last week replaced it?"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "where-i-am"
        }
      }
    }
